    {"id":"tension_body","type":"text","x":760,"y":188,"width":790,"height":150,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#374151","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":0,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":null,"seed":100014,"version":1,"versionNonce":1,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":null,"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"Paper = a visible grid page. CAPI = 42 sequential screens.\nThe construct that keeps the row-feel (one combined screen) is the fragile one:\n#617, #805, #818 all came from DisplayTogether block-exit mechanics.\nWording/scripts/periods/totals are NOW paper-verbatim (R4-R6 fixes) —\nthe remaining question is the FLOW. Even the paper's opening script is\nambiguous: 'First... then...' describes a two-pass flow nobody implements.","fontSize":14,"fontFamily":3,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"originalText":"Paper = a visible grid page. CAPI = 42 sequential screens.\nThe construct that keeps the row-feel (one combined screen) is the fragile one:\n#617, #805, #818 all came from DisplayTogether block-exit mechanics.\nWording/scripts/periods/totals are NOW paper-verbatim (R4-R6 fixes) —\nthe remaining question is the FLOW. Even the paper's opening script is\nambiguous: 'First... then...' describes a two-pass flow nobody implements.","lineHeight":1.35,"baseline":14},

